{"title":"Career roadmap · Graduate Engineer Trainee","role":"Graduate Engineer Trainee","summary":"A Graduate Engineer Trainee (GET) is typically an entry-level engineering position through which a fresh mechanical-engineering graduate rotates through functions such as production, maintenance, quality, manufacturing, design, projects and operations before moving into a specialised engineering role.","facts":{"Starts":"Year 1","Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. (Bachelor of Technology / Engineering)","Timeline assumption":"Four-year B.Tech/B.E. beginning in 2026 and graduating around 2030."},"about":[{"label":"Career-route check","text":"Graduate Engineer Trainee is a directly accessible entry route for Mechanical Engineering graduates. Unlike a narrowly specialised role, GET is a training designation, so the eventual career depends heavily on the department and industry in which the trainee is placed."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[{"period":"2026–2030","question":"What can I enter now?","output":"Build mechanical fundamentals, CAD, manufacturing, materials, quality, maintenance and industrial problem-solving skills."},{"period":"2030–2035","question":"How should I specialise?","output":"Use the GET rotation to choose production, design, quality, maintenance, projects, automotive, HVAC or manufacturing."},{"period":"2035–2040","question":"How should I evolve?","output":"Move toward Senior Engineer, Lead Engineer, Project/Production leadership or specialist engineering roles."},{"period":"2040–2046","question":"How can I remain relevant?","output":"Combine mechanical expertise with automation, simulation, data, sustainability and digital manufacturing."}],"sections":[{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from","Proof of progress","Gap it moves"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 1"},{"text":"Engineering mathematics, physics, engineering drawing and basic mechanics"},{"text":"NPTEL","url":"https://nptel.ac.in/"},{"text":"Engineering-drawing portfolio + solved mechanics problems"},{"text":"Analytical thinking"}],[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 2"},{"text":"Materials, thermodynamics and basic manufacturing"},{"text":"NPTEL","url":"https://nptel.ac.in/"},{"text":"Material-selection and manufacturing case study"},{"text":"Technical foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 1"},{"text":"Strength of materials, fluid mechanics and machine elements"},{"text":"MIT OpenCourseWare · NPTEL","url":"https://ocw.mit.edu/"},{"text":"Design calculations for a mechanical component"},{"text":"Analytical thinking"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 2"},{"text":"AutoCAD/SolidWorks/CAD + manufacturing processes"},{"text":"Autodesk Learning · SOLIDWORKS Education","url":"https://www.autodesk.com/learn"},{"text":"3D part, assembly and manufacturing drawing"},{"text":"Digital literacy"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 1"},{"text":"Production, quality, maintenance and industrial engineering"},{"text":"ASQ","url":"https://asq.org/"},{"text":"Quality-control case study + process-improvement project"},{"text":"Execution"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 2"},{"text":"GD&T, FMEA, root-cause analysis and lean manufacturing"},{"text":"ASME · NPTEL","url":"https://www.asme.org/"},{"text":"FMEA + 5-Why/RCA + process-improvement report"},{"text":"Problem solving"}],[{"text":"Year 4 Sem 1"},{"text":"Industrial internship + ERP/project exposure"},{"text":"Siemens Digital Industries","url":"https://www.siemens.com/global/en/products/automation.html"},{"text":"Internship report with measurable engineering contribution"},{"text":"Ownership"}],[{"text":"Year 4 Sem 2"},{"text":"Capstone project + GET/placement preparation"},{"text":"SAE International","url":"https://www.sae.org/"},{"text":"Working prototype/design + technical presentation"},{"text":"Communication, leadership"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Core technical subjects to master"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Engineering mechanics"},{"text":"Strength of materials"},{"text":"Thermodynamics"},{"text":"Fluid mechanics"},{"text":"Heat transfer"},{"text":"Engineering materials"},{"text":"Manufacturing processes"},{"text":"Machine design"},{"text":"CAD/CAM"},{"text":"Metrology"},{"text":"Industrial engineering"},{"text":"Production engineering"},{"text":"Quality engineering"},{"text":"Maintenance engineering"},{"text":"Engineering economics and project fundamentals"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Four-year honours variant"},{"type":"p","text":"Use the additional year for industry internships, advanced CAD/CAE, manufacturing automation, robotics, digital manufacturing or a research/industry capstone."},{"type":"h","text":"Specialisation"},{"type":"table","header":["Lane","Core stack","Learn from","Senior role it leads to"],"rows":[[{"text":"Production Engineering"},{"text":"Manufacturing, lean, OEE, process optimisation"},{"text":"ASQ","url":"https://asq.org/"},{"text":"Production Manager"}],[{"text":"Mechanical Design"},{"text":"CAD, GD&T, FEA, machine design"},{"text":"SOLIDWORKS","url":"https://www.solidworks.com/"},{"text":"Senior Design Engineer"}],[{"text":"Quality Engineering"},{"text":"SPC, FMEA, RCA, quality systems"},{"text":"ASQ","url":"https://asq.org/"},{"text":"Quality Manager"}],[{"text":"Maintenance"},{"text":"Reliability, TPM, preventive/predictive maintenance"},{"text":"SMRP","url":"https://smrp.org/"},{"text":"Maintenance Manager"}],[{"text":"Manufacturing Automation"},{"text":"PLC, robotics, CNC, MES"},{"text":"Siemens Automation","url":"https://www.siemens.com/global/en/products/automation.html"},{"text":"Manufacturing/Automation Engineer"}],[{"text":"Project Engineering"},{"text":"Planning, procurement, estimation, execution"},{"text":"PMI","url":"https://www.pmi.org/"},{"text":"Project Manager"}],[{"text":"Automotive"},{"text":"Vehicle systems, manufacturing, testing"},{"text":"SAE International","url":"https://www.sae.org/"},{"text":"Automotive Engineering Lead"}]]},{"type":"note","label":"Evolve and stay relevant, 2035–2046","text":"Mechanical engin